<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panchayat</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as panchayats</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A panchayat is a traditional village council in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>, typically composed of elders. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> panchayats managed agrarian disputes and customary law. They worked alongside provincial officials responsible for justice, revenue and defence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panchayat.jpg" alt="Panchayat" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shijualex at Malayalam Wikipedia · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muhamma_grama_panchayath.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
